Step 5 – Understanding the Code
onMessage
chrome.runtime.onMessage.addListener(...)

Registers an event listener.

Every time any extension component sends a message,

the background receives it.

message

Contains

{
   type:"ASK_AI",
   prompt:"Explain Kubernetes"
}
sender

Information about

Popup
Content Script
Side Panel
sendResponse()

Used to send data back.

Example

sendResponse({
    success:true,
    response:"Hello"
})
return true

Always return

true

when responding asynchronously.

Even though we're responding immediately, it's a good habit because later we'll call APIs.

